{
    "id": 45,
    "title": "Migrations at publish, copied first",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-14 (decisions/0162, amending 0145 §6): a release's migrations run as Publish's first step, before its files go live, and a failure stops the publish with the error in its record. A compressed copy of the tables each migration touches is kept 14 days, listed on System Configuration → Database updates with Restore. A migration that changes rows needs a data_reason and never runs without its copy. Roll back records what a release's migrations made as its leftovers, listed on Database updates (Pulse case and the monthly unused-schema check come in release 2).",
